2 CONT    In january, 1917, Ole had a serious accident while grinding
2 CONT
2 CONT feed for his cattle. It was a cold day and he had his mittens on.
2 CONT
2 CONT JacobPeterson, who was helping him in the granary, had just taken
2 CONT
2 CONT a sack to the feedhouse while Ole was operating the mill. Somehow
2 CONT
2 CONT the mitten got caught in the pully and the left hand was drawn be-
2 CONT
2 CONT tween the two grinding discs up toward the elbow. It was crushed
2 CONT
2 CONT and felt burned and wrenched. Dr. Amos Flaten came and made arrange-
2 CONT
2 CONT ments to get him to the Grand Forks hospital. The accident had hap-
2 CONT
2 CONT pened about three o'clock and since the train left for Grand Forks
2 CONT
2 CONT at five there was no tinie to spare in gettirrg hial to the train.
