2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie Ommedal, 100, Maxbass, North Dakota, died Monday, June 5, 2017, at a Mohall nursing home, Mohall, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born May 28, 1917, in Brander Township, Bottineau County, to Jorgen and Sophie (Lerfald) Tengesdal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She attended grade school and high school at Brander Consolidated School. She graduated as valedictorian of Brander Consolidated School Class of 1934. She worked for relatives during her teen years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie attended Bemis College of Commerce, Minot. She won a six-month scholarship to attend the college through a contest by making words out of the letters in the name of the college. She was employed as a secretary for the North
2 CONC  Dakota Legislature in Bismarck. She worked five years for the Bottineau County Treasurer’s Office.  From 1942 to 1945, she worked for J.C. Penney in Spokane, Wash. Following this, she returned to the farm to help her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie married Ole Ommedal, a Norwegian immigrant, on Nov. 23, 1952, at Betania Lutheran Church, rural Maxbass. They lived in Seattle, Wash., their first winter together. The following spring, they returned to North Dakota to join
2 CONC  Tollef Tengesdal in farming the Pauline Brackelsberg land near Loraine. They farmed there for over four years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1957, Ole and Sophie purchased the Fred Piquette farm in Brander Township where they farmed and raised their five children. Sophie was famous for her homemade buns. Ole passed away in March of 1994 and Sophie remained on the fa
2 CONC rm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie was a member of Betania Lutheran Church, rural Maxbass, and served as organist for many years at both Betania and Holden Lutheran Churches. When Betania Lutheran Church closed, she joined English Lutheran Church, Maxbass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: daughters, Nancy (Barry) Land, Fargo, North Dakota;  Diane (Tom) Nyberg, Grand Forks, North Dakota; 
2 CONT Julie (Darcy) Johnson, Watford City, North Dakota;  sons, Duane (Laila Fick) Ommedal, Maxbass, North Dakota; 
2 CONT  Dwight (Peggy Thorenson) Ommedal, Maxbass, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT And grandchildren, Benjamin Land, Sarah (Tyler) VanDeVelde, Miranda (Booker) Roy, Alyssa Nyberg, Rebecca (Jake) Peterson, Joran Johnson, Reese Johnson; great-grandchildren, Axel and Finn Roy, and Grace VanDeVelde.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is also survived by sisters-in-law, Pearl Tengesdal, Maxbass, North Dakota;  Melba Tengesdal, Appleton, Wisconsin;  dear friend, Lou Heil, Hazen, North Dakota; and numerous nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie was preceded in death by her parents; husband; infant sister, Sadie; siblings, Jens, Sadie, Nels, Amanda, Roy and Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *Jorgen Jensen Tengesdal (1867 - 1933)
2 CONT *Sophie Lerfald Tengesdal (1879 - 1957)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *Ole Matias Ommedal (1924 - 1994)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT *Sadie Josephine Tengesdal (1903 - 1903)
2 CONT *Jens Sigvart Tengesdal (1906 - 1981)
2 CONT *Sadie Jonetta Tengesdal Morrison (1907 - 1959)
2 CONT *Nels Joseph Tengesdal (1910 - 1991)
2 CONT *Roy Albert Tengesdal (1913 - 1999)
2 CONT *Sophie Tengesdal Ommedal (1917 - 2017)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Betania Cemetery  Brander Township Bottineau County North Dakota.
2 CONT ----
