1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1930 - Brander Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota. (age 8)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Peter Nans Joren Tengesdal, son of Jorgen and Sophie (Lerfald) Tengesdal, died peacefully into God's embrace, Nov. 21, 2007, at age 86.   Burial in First Lutheran Church Cemetery, Poulsbo, Washington. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter was born Oct. 29, 1921, on the family farmstead near Maxbass, North Dakota, and was baptized Dec. 4. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He affirmed his baptism through Confirmation Sept. 1, 1935. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After graduation from Brander School, he entered the North Dakota School of Forestry in 1939. Two years later he enlisted in the U.S. Navy and served as an ensign on the U.S.S. Nevada until he entered Concordia College, Moorhead, 
2 CONC Minn., in 1946, where he majored in business administration and minored in English. While employed as dean of boys at Dakota Lutheran High School, Minot, Peter met Melba Tenney. They were married Aug. 12, 1951.
2 CONT
2 CONT Called to pastoral ministry, Peter graduated from Luther Seminary in St. Paul, Minnesota, in 1954, and served three prairie Lutheran churches near Williston: Our Saviour's, Buford-Trenton Home Mission and Rosseland. In 1960 the Te
2 CONC ngesdal family moved to Seattle, where Peter served as assistant pastor in charge of youth and education at Ballard First Lutheran Church. In 1967 they ferried across the Puget Sound to Poulsbo, Washington, ("Little Norway") where
2 CONC  Peter served as senior pastor of First Lutheran Church for nearly 20 years. Retirement took Peter and his wife to Tacoma, Wash., where he served as a visitation pastor for Emmanuel Lutheran and then back to Poulsbo First Lutheran
2 CONC  as Visitation Pastor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter modeled a life of pastoral care and compassion for those less fortunate. He preached grace. If a sermon didn't lift up God's grace, he concluded that it was one which shouldn't have been preached. In addition to work, he enj
2 CONC oyed long, annual U.S./Canada vacations with his wife and four children. He and Melba also enjoyed travel to Hawaii, Israel, Egypt, Morocco, Norway, other European countries and the Lawrence Welk resort in Escondido, California. B
2 CONC eing outdoors and growing gladiolas, roses, carnations and vegetables brought Peter great joy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife, Melba; his sons, Jeff (Barb), Appleton, Wisconsin and Mark, Plano, Texas; his daughter, Patricia (David) Siburg, Fontanelle, Nebraska.
2 CONT
2 CONT And his grandchildren, Timothy, Thomas, Tamara Siburg,Joren and Britta Tengesdal; a sister, Sophie Ommedal, Maxbass; two "adopted" daughters, Gail Hovick and Margo Holm; and two "adopted" grandchildren, Matthew and Jennifer Holm.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; three sisters; three brothers; and son, Daniel.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * U.S. Social Security Death Index
2 CONT * Peter N Tengesdal
2 CONT * Birth:	Oct 29 1921
2 CONT * Death:	Nov 21 2007
2 CONT * Last residence:	Poulsbo, Washington
2 CONT ----
