1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Athalia Ivesdal and Reuben Hammer met in high school and were fondly acquainted.  Athalia was the daughter of Lars Ivesdal and Martha Haug Ivesdal.  Reuben moved to Oregon with his parents but they kept in touch an
2 CONC d she soon joined him geographically as well as matrimonially.  They moved to Los Angeles during the depression and had two children, Marian Adele and Richard Allen "Dick."  They soon moved to the suburbs in the newly developed co
2 CONC mmunity of Lakewood, CA, where their children grew and thrived.  Reuben opened a Richfield gas station on the north-west corner of Lakewood Boulevard and Artesia Streets in Paramount and Athalia completed her teaching certificate.
2 CONC   She taught first grade in Lomita for many years prior to her retirement.  Both parents doted on their children having had them later in life.  Marian married a dairy farmer, Corrie Vanderham, and her children were the light of R
2 CONC euben and Athalia's life.  They took vacations back to the Ivesdahl family farm in North Dakota, saved, lived frugally and lived out their lives in a modest and comfortable manner.  They will forever be remembered by their seven g
2 CONC randchildren and many great-grandchildren.  It can truly be said that Reuben and Athalia's lives revolved around their family to whom they were dearly devoted. Inscription: Beloved Mother, Grandmother and Great Grandmother
2 CONT
2 CONT               ATHALIA I. HAMMER
2 CONT
2 CONT                  1903 - 1997
