2 DATE 1917
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry A. Christopherson, 90, of Grand Forks, passed away on Monday, August 13, 2007, at Altru Hospital in Grand Forks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Ardell Christopherson was born December 21, 1916, at rural Edinburg, North Dakota, to Karinius and Karina Christopherson. He attended school in Lampton Township, completed three years of high school in Edinburg, North Dakota
2 CONC , and graduated from high school in 1934 from the Lutheran Bible School in Grand Forks, North Dakota. He attended business college in Minneapolis, Minnesota, for two years and relocated to Los Angeles, California, in 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served in the US Army from 1945-46. He worked as an accountant for several companies in the Los Angeles area. In 1990 he moved to Grand Forks following his retirement from the Allison Company.
2 CONT
2 CONT He resided at Parkwood Place from 1996 until his death on Monday, August 13, 2007. He was the last surviving member of his immediate family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry is survived by his sisters-in-law Mabel Christopherson of Wheaton, Illinois, and Dordene Strecker of Bend, Oregon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; two sisters, Inez Ulberg and Thelma Markholt; and six brothers, Clarence, Alton, Alver, Leonard, Clifford and Raymond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was a dear and special uncle who will be missed at family gatherings.
2 CONT
2 CONT FUNERAL SERVICES: 2:00 p.m., Friday, August 17, 2007, at Amundson Funeral Home 2975 S. 42nd St. in Grand Forks.
2 CONT
2 CONT VISITATION: One hour prior to the funeral service at Amundson's.
2 CONT
2 CONT INTERMENT: Memorial Park South Cemetery, Grand Forks, ND
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.amundsonfuneralhome.com/sitemaker/sites/amunds1/obit.cgi?user=henry-christopherson#
