1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NDPDI died 08/19/1960 in Ward County, 78 Years; born 08/29/1881. Residence - Bottineau County.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * 1900 - Township 160-80, Bottineau County, North Dakota. (farm laborer)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Peter Lerfald was born August 29, 1881 at West Concord, Minnesota the son of Nels and Jonetta Lerfald.  He moved with his parents to Galesburg, North Dakota in 1890, and in 1900 came with them to Newborg Township, where he filed o
2 CONC n a relinquishedment on a quarter mile from his parents homestead.  A man named Wicklund ran all the way to Bottineau to record the file for him and got there before another fellow (also filing on the same land) drove a team and b
2 CONC uggy.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1914, Peter married Ottlile Johnson, born September 18, 1894 in Traill County, North Dakota, the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Casper Johnson.  Peter and Ottile had one daughter, Pearl (Mrs Embert Sveum).  Ottile died in 1916. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter farmed and was active in township affairs and the Holden Lutheran Church.  In 1948 he married Mrs. Anna Vetsvag of Upham and moved into Bottineau.  She was the mother of three daughters, Angie (Mrs. Clayton Kitzman),  Doris 
2 CONC (Mrs. John Homen) and Henrietta (Mrs. Lloyd Mickelson).
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter died in 1960 and Anna died in 1979.
2 CONT ----
