2 CONT ----
2 CONT * 1910 - Township 160-80, Bottineau County, North Dakota.
2 CONT * 1910 - Newborg Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota.
2 CONT * 1920 - Newborg Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota.
2 CONT * 1930 - Newborg Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota.
2 CONT * 1940 - Newborg Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota. (widowed)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mrs. Mathilda Wedar, 91, of Minot, North Dakota, one of the last remaining area pioneers, died Tuesday, May 27, 1975.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Mathilda Lerfald, February 25, 1884 at West Concord, Minnesota.  
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 6, she moved with her parents to Galesburg, North Dakota.  In 1900 they moved to Bottieau County.  She married Gust Wedar on February 14, 1903.  They farmed in Newborg Township, Bottineau County.  Her husband died in
2 CONC  1936.  She continued living on the farm until moving to Minot in 1963.  Since then, she had lived with her daughters.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She is a Charter Member of Holden Lutheran Church and the Ladies Aid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by two daughters, Mrs. Clara Larkin and Mrs. Vernice (George) Wahus both of Minot, North Dakota; a son Noble of rural Maxbass; eight grandchildren; 16 great grandchildren; and three sisters, Mrs. Regina Wedar, Grea
2 CONC t Falls, Montana;  Amanda Lefald, Maxbass, North Dakota;  and Mrs. Harold Ahlstrom of Minneapolis, Minnesota. 
2 CONT ----
