1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1920:	Newborg Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota
2 CONT * 1930:	Fort Benton, Chouteau County, Montana
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mr and Mrs Claus Wedar of Loma, Montana observed their golden wedding anniversary at a reception recently at their home.                      
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple was married February 14, 1912, at Holden Lutheran Church, Eckman, North Dakota. They have been Loma area residents since homesteading there shortly after their marriage.                      
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wedars have two children, Mrs Irvin Gardner of Great Falls, Montana and Alvin Wedar of Menlo Park, California and four grandchildren. A daughter, Mrs Robert (Judith) Donaldson, died in 1947. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Regina A. Wedar, 93, 264 19th Ave. NW, Great Falls, Montana died Friday in a local hospital. Burial will be in Highland Cemetery, Great Falls, Montana.            
2 CONT
2 CONT Regina was born at West Concord, Minnesota.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She attended school at West Concord, Minnesota until she was nine years old and her family moved to Maxbass, North Dakota.  She and Claus T. Wedar were married at Maxbass, North Dakota in February 1912.  She moved to Great Falls, 
2 CONC Montana aft his death in July 1966.          
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her daughter, Mrs Irvin (Ruth) Gardner, Great Falls, Montana;  a son Alvin Wedar, Menio Park, California.  
2 CONT
2 CONT And three grandchildren, two great grandchildren.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Regina is also survived by her sister, Hilda Ahlstrom, Minneapolis, Minnesota.    
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter, Juith Donaldson, preceded her death in 1946.
2 CONT ----
