1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ole Ommedal was born on April 8, 1924 at Bjerkreim, Norway. He attended college in Norway and taught school for two years before coming to North Dakota in the spring of 1948.  He was employed on the Milton Fossum f
2 CONC arm in Newborg Township, Bottineau County, worked in Minot, and in the state of Washington before moving to the Pauline Brackelsberg farm near Loraine in Renville County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole and Sophie Tengesdal, daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Jorgen Tengesdal, were married in November 1952.  Sophie graduated from Brander High School and attended business college for six months.  She was employed at the Bottineau County
2 CONC  Treasurer's office for a number of years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1957, the Ommedals moved to the former Fred Piquette farm in Brander Township.
