2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE I'm not in this picture because I was on my honeymoon.  This picture was taken the day after our wedding.  Jack Anderson and Faye Edeal were married on May 9, 1953.    I was sorry I couldn't be with the family but I think you all 
3 CONC understand why.
3 CONT     Alta Faye Anderson-Atkinson
2 NOTE Your welcome!  I received and invitation from Wendy to join the site.  I've sent invitations to many of the California Edeals.  My brother Wallace just passed away last Friday at 72.  We had some great visits with him and his last
3 CONC  two days were actually a great time of visiting with family.  He and I were very close.  It was a tough 3 months, but now he's in no more pain and dancing with the angels as well as reuniting with all the former relatives and fri
3 CONC ends,  It was last week when I nofified Wendy and the other cousins that she informed me of this site. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Last August 2008, my wife and I spent 3 weeks in Sweden and 1 week in Norway.  Her sister lives in Stockholm and we also visited some of her Swedish relatives while there.  I've checked the phone pages in Sweden and found several 
3 CONC Odil', Edell, and Edel in southern Sweden, but that was after we got home to the US. The Edeal name seems to have been spelled at least 4 ways.  There were no "Edeals" over there but lots of the other three spellings.  I hope to c
3 CONC ontinue the research.  It seems our Great great grandfather was from Jonkoping in Smalland area of southern Sweden.  It is beautiful country, but all of Sweden is beautiful.
3 CONT
3 CONT When in Oslo Norway we stayed with Alice Husby who's Mother was a cousin of our grandmother Lena Edeal.  Lena's  maiden name was Reime and she was born and lived in Lyngdal Norway until 11 when she came over on a ship with some fa
3 CONC mily to the US.  They settled in Nebraska and that's where she met Arthur Edeal our grandfather.  
3 CONT
3 CONT Alice Husby is 84 and very healthy and active.  She was so glad to see us and show us around.  I know she was not from the Edeal side, but she too is an accomplished artist and painted some on fine china.  She's very humble about 
3 CONC her work and would never brag, but she's sold a lot in art galleries in Oslo. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Alice had previously visited the US in 2003 and attended our California Edeal family reunion which my wife and I host her in Mt. Hermon, CA.  You can look up Mt. Hermon on the web.  It is a Christian Retreat which has been here si
3 CONC nce 1906.  My wife works here and I used to work for the Mt. Hermon Association, but have been a Marriage counselor for the past 25 years.   
3 CONT
3 CONT Yes, that is Mary Edeal holding Scott in her lap.  My brother Wally and sister Alta Fay were not in that picture for some reason.  Well that's a lot.  The older I become the more important these family tree's become.  Thx for your
3 CONC  reply.  I am only sorry we never got to connect with our Nebraska and other relatives until now.  
3 CONT
3 CONT We Edeals are few and far between.  My brother and I together have 6 Edeal sons and they have a total of three Edeal sons so far so it looks like we won't become extinct in California.  Ron Edeal  
2 NOTE Thank you for adding people and photos.
3 CONT We Russell Edeal and Kay ,visited Dorothy Bloom Behrens this past Friday, bringing her \birthday greetings.  She has not changed--very hospital, neatly groomed, feminine,gracious. She told us 3 times, "It is so good to see the two
3 CONC  of you, or It is so good that you came.  She resides at Christian homes in Holdrege, NE.  While we were there we met Mary (Payne) Johnson, also a resident.  She is a cousin of George & Louise Edeal who are children of Henry & Jen
3 CONC nie Edeal.
3 CONT We know Mary was an accomplished artist and loved the area of china painting...a handsome woman with many friends.
3 CONT Have a blessed day.
3 CONT I loved the photo with children ages..seeing Wendy and Scott who we have met and cherish the bond.  Is Mary the one "holding" Scott?  
3 CONT Our daughter is named Mary...now Reimers. 
