1 NOTE {geni:about_me} To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/59012928/olai_t-helland
2 CONT
2 CONT Famer Taken By Death Tuesday
2 CONT Binford Man Came To Griggs In 1904 from Mt. Vernon, South Dakota
2 CONT O. T. Helland, familiar figure in community life of Binford and surrounding
2 CONT area, passed away suddenly at his home near that village at the noon hour
2 CONT Tuesday.
2 CONT He had been a resident of Griggs county since 1904, coming here from Mr.
2 CONT Vernon, S.D. During the last several years he had been in poor health which
2 CONT his advanced age was unable to shake off. He was in his eight-fifth year at
2 CONT the time of his death.
2 CONT Olai T. Helland was born in Thime Logn, Jaderen, Norway, October 1, 1850.
2 CONT in 1874 he was married to bergitta Lindahl and to this union three children
2 CONT were born, one dying in infancy. His first wife died in 1891, the same day
2 CONT upon which a son of two years old also died.
2 CONT In 1893 Helland came to this country with his two children, settling at Mt.
2 CONT Vernon, S.D., where he resided until 1904. There he married Anna Danielson
2 CONT and came subsequently to the farm near Binford where he has lived since.
2 CONT He is survived by his wife; one son, Teodore of Mt. Vernon, S.D., a
2 CONT daughtrer, Mrs. F. Froiland of Glendive, Montana; and a sister, Mrs. J. L.
2 CONT Rapstad of Big Timber, Montana.
2 CONT Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Courier, Cooperstown, ND, June, 1935
